{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-06 current-main revalidation (2026-08-18): planning worktree HEAD and origin/main are both `3b34d8b449ae4b56a5da8fb434aa75df7194b0c4`; worktree clean. RP-01/RP-04 landed changes touch adjacent LLM/config surfaces but not the RP-06 selection/execution/checkpoint defects.\n\nReran the four existing checkout-local probes against current main:\n- `rp06-pass1-kernel-probe.py`: 3/3 routing divergences remain (disabled built-in still scheduled, effective project DET invisible to code-review detector selection, nonmatching project LLM criterion still runs).\n- `rp06-failure-checkpoint-probe.py`: transient local failure is still persisted as `[]` and replayed as a clean resumed checkpoint with no healthy retry.\n- `rp06-checkpoint-key-probe.py`: prompt/routing/posture changes still produce the same checkpoint key and replay old output.\n- `rp06-review-kernel-probe.py`: code review still ignores the supplied zero-budget probe, aborts before later independent work, loses a typed partial result, and reads split packaged/effective policy.\n\nThis confirms D6.1 remains a real product choice rather than being superseded by current main. Recommendation remains parity-first: typed truthful unit outcomes and success-only digest-complete checkpoints now, while preserving each gate's current-run call/verdict projection during the structural cutover; separately review any later posture-aware normalization. No production or tracked files changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787072071345531001,"uuid":"060b0dd0-9025-46e7-9a42-af0490850093"}